  "text": "SYDNEY.\n20th March, 1946.\nC.H. McFadyen, Esq.,\nSecondary Industries Division,\n119h1114. St. St. 2.S.W.\nDear Mr. McFadyen,\nMr. Elvery has told me that you\nare leaving Sydney to take up the position\nof Deputy Director, Secondary Industries\nDivision, in Victoria.\nI would like to offer you my\ncongratulations on your appointment and to\nextend to you my best wishes for the future.\nI also want to take the oppor-\ntunity of thanking you for the great co-\noperation you have extended to the Bank\nover recent months, and to reiterate what\nI said at the meeting with the Secondary\nIndustries Commission,\nthat the Industrial\nFinance Department could not have got along\nwithout the help of both you and your\nDepartment in Sydney.\nWith kind regards,\nYours sincerely,\nanarmstrong\n/ AGREED TO INVESTIGATE AND REPORT ON ALL REQUESTS TO THE MEN IMDUSTRIAL\nFINANCE REPARTMENT OF THE COmmONERKTH BANK By INMUSTRIALISTS FOR FiNANCiAL\nASSISTANCE ARE TO GO SO / MAR TO ESTABLISH A COMPETENT BODY OF TECHNiCAL\nINTESTIGATORS IN MHICH TASK I WAS GiVEN ALL POSSIBLE ASSISTANCE BY\nMA J.K.L.ENSEN (HOW SIR JONN JENSEN) SECRETARY TEP! OF MUNITIONS. / GATHEREO\nAROUNO ME A SPLENDIA STAFF OF COST INTESTIORTORS RAG ENGINBERS OF MANY\nCLASSES, INCLURING ELECTRICAL, CHEMICAL, CIVIL, MECHANIAI AND MARINE. OUR REPORTS\nHERE THOROUGM AND APPARENTAY PLERSEN THE BANK OFFICIANS.\nMARiE\nJANE • RAViO\nMARIE\nLINAR",
